Copied existing data using this query and converted existing NULLS to 'unknown'. This was done to not remove rows or columns where NULL values were common. 
SELECT 
    hotel, is_canceled, lead_time, arrival_date_year, arrival_date_month,
    arrival_date_week_number, arrival_date_day_of_month, stays_in_weekend_nights,
    stays_in_week_nights, adults, COALESCE(children, 0), babies, meal,
    COALESCE(country, 'Unknown'), market_segment, distribution_channel,
    is_repeated_guest, previous_cancellations, previous_bookings_not_canceled,
    reserved_room_type, assigned_room_type, booking_changes, deposit_type,
    COALESCE(agent, 'Unknown'), COALESCE(company, 'Unknown'),
    days_in_waiting_list, customer_type, adr, required_car_parking_spaces,
    total_of_special_requests, reservation_status, reservation_status_date
FROM hotelbook_old;

Dropped old table using: 
DROP TABLE hotelbook_old;

After refreshing the updates from the prior queries I was still seeing NULL values. The below includes UPDATE as a way to commit prior adjustments. Needed to TRIM to remove beginning and ending white spaces. 
   UPDATE hotelbook
SET 
    country = CASE 
        WHEN country IS NULL OR TRIM(country) = '' OR LOWER(TRIM(country)) = 'null' THEN 'Unknown' 
        ELSE country 
    END,
    agent = CASE 
        WHEN agent IS NULL OR TRIM(agent) = '' OR LOWER(TRIM(agent)) = 'null' THEN 'Unknown' 
        ELSE agent 
    END,
    company = CASE 
        WHEN company IS NULL OR TRIM(company) = '' OR LOWER(TRIM(company)) = 'null' THEN 'Unknown' 
        ELSE company 
    END,
    children = CASE 
        WHEN children IS NULL OR TRIM(CAST(children AS TEXT)) = '' OR LOWER(TRIM(CAST(children AS TEXT))) = 'null' THEN 0 
        ELSE children 
    END;
